As the ocean's waves crashed onto the shore,
A symphony of sound, a dance of the tide;
The water's edge, a canvas, ever-changing, yet serene.

The sand, a stage, where the waves' rhythmic beat,
 Created patterns, a poetry, wild and free;
The waves' caress, a gentle touch, a soothing melody,
As the ocean's roar, a chorus, sang in harmony.

The tide pulled back, revealing a poem, hidden in plain sight;
A message, encoded, in the waves' ebb and flow;
A language, universal, yet mysterious, and yet, so clear;
A poem, that spoke of life, of change, of the eternal cycle.

The waves' patterns, a reflection, of the human heart;
A dance of contradictions, of light and dark, of hope and despair;
A poem, that whispered secrets, of the universe's design;
A mystery, that beckoned, to the soul's deepest core.

The poem's meaning, a question, that echoed through the mind;
A riddle, that whispered, "What lies beneath the surface, is it not divine?";
The waves' poetry, a mirror, reflecting our deepest fears;
A reminder, that the unknown, is where the magic appears.

As the ocean's waves, continued to ebb and flow,
The poem's message, remained, a mystery, yet to be told;
A poem, that spoke of the human condition;
A reflection, of our hopes, our dreams, our deepest desires.

The interrobang, a punctuation mark, that questioned and exclaimed;
A symbol, that embodied, the paradox of life's extremes;
A reminder, that the ocean's poetry, was a reflection, of our own;
A dance, of contradictions, of light and dark, of hope and despair, and yet, so serene.

The poem's meaning, a question, that still remains;
A mystery, that beckons, to the soul's deepest core;
A reminder, that the ocean's poetry, is a reflection, of our own;
A dance, of contradictions, of light and dark, of hope and despair, and yet, so free.
